# This file exists to stop ONE class of false accusation, discovered during a
# documentation-rewrite session:
#
#   content/v1.4.5/zh/api/_index.md was silently converted LF -> CRLF. The
#   resulting diff read "+93 -68", which looks exactly like a wholesale rewrite
#   of the title, description, H1 and every section heading. It was not:
#   after normalising line endings the file differed by 13 added lines and
#   ZERO deletions. Two more files converted in the same batch.
#
#   A verifier read that diffstat and reported "this worker rewrote the
#   headings". Both the accusation and its rebuttal were wrong, and the whole
#   round was spent re-deriving it.
#
# `core.autocrlf` was false on the machine that did it, which is the SAFE
# setting -- but it says nothing about the repository's convention, so each
# tool re-decided for itself. That is the gap this closes.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SCOPE IS DELIBERATELY NARROW. Do not widen it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Measured before writing this rule:
#
#   tracked files in HEAD          132,832
#   text files with CRLF in HEAD    63,455   <- 47.8%
#
# The repository is full of CRLF in git history, largely under `_audit_l1/`
# (mirror/selfcheck trees). A blanket `* text=auto eol=lf` would normalise all
# 63,455 of them on the next commit that touched them, burying real edits under
# a repo-wide diff. So the rule is scoped to the trees this project authors.
#
# Verified: with this file in place,
#   git check-attr text eol -- content/v1.4.5/zh/api/_index.md
#     -> text: auto   eol: lf
#
# If the historical trees are ever migrated, migrate them in their own commit
# with `--renormalize`, and review that diff on its own terms. Do not fold it
# into unrelated work.

# Documentation this project authors. Also the only tree measured clean of
# legacy CRLF at the time of writing.
content/**    text=auto eol=lf

# Tooling and gates: short, diff-reviewed, churn would hide real logic changes.
tools/**      text=auto eol=lf

# Deliberately NOT covered: _audit_l1/, _withdrawn/, public/, and anything else
# carried over from before this rule existed. Those are historical; normalising
# them is a separate, explicitly-scoped migration.

# Binary assets -- eol normalisation must never touch these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.mp4  binary

# Patches and diffs carry meaning in their line structure.
*.patch text eol=lf
*.diff  text eol=lf
